    <!-- THIS IS NOT A POLISH TRANSLATION. Every value here is UKRAINIAN.

         The app's UI is Ukrainian (CONTEXT.md). This directory exists for one
         reason: on a Polish-system device Android would otherwise voice
         Material3's own Polish strings ("Zamknij arkusz", "Uchwyt do
         przeciągania") through TalkBack. A `pl` qualifier holding Ukrainian
         text wins over the library's Polish and keeps the spoken language
         coherent — that is the whole purpose (#371).

         #1385 — it used to be a MIXTURE: five such Ukrainian overrides plus 31
         genuine Polish translations added for app features. The result on a
         Polish device was half Ukrainian, half Polish on the same screen
         («Książki» beside «Полиці», «Mój rok w książkach» beside «Збережене»).
         A partially translated language is worse than an untranslated one: the
         untranslated one falls back to one coherent language.

         So: do NOT add Polish translations here. If Polish is ever wanted as a
         real language, it must be complete — see #1387/#1388/#1389 — and it
         would need its own qualifier strategy, not this override file. -->

